THE FOUR TARGETS, chosen so that one leg answers four different questions at once:

  192.168.48.5    routed out vlan48, a DIFFERENT interface from the one the request arrives on
                  => the proxy-ARP case.  MUST be answered when the feature is on.
  10.99.99.99     no route at all (`Gateway of last resort is not set`)
                  => MUST NOT be answered, on or off.  Proves the DUT does not answer blindly.
  192.168.10.78   inside vlan10's own subnet, i.e. the SAME interface the request arrives on
                  => MUST NOT be answered by proxy ARP; that is `ip local-proxy-arp`'s domain
                  and is case T43849.  Proves the two features are distinct.
  192.168.10.1    the DUT's OWN address on the receiving interface
                  => the INSTRUMENT CONTROL.  MUST be answered in every leg.  Without it, "no
                  reply" cannot be told apart from "the instrument is not working".

