VERDICT: PASS -- with `ip proxy-arp` on vlan10 the DUT answers ARP requests arriving on vlan10
for an address reachable via vlan48, with its OWN MAC (e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43), where the identical
request drew no reply with the feature off; it answers for NEITHER an address it has no route to
NOR an address on the receiving interface's own subnet, so it is gated on reachability and
bounded away from local proxy ARP; the behaviour is proven per-interface in both directions (the
vlan48 side is silent until the same command is added there, then answers); the proxied address
is genuinely reachable, with all 5 crafted frames addressed to the DUT's MAC emerging on vlan48
addressed to the real owner; removal clears running-config and both wires; and the whole matrix
reproduces frame for frame after a reboot.  Every leg carried its own instrument control (the
DUT's own address, answered in all of them), so each "no reply" is a measurement rather than an
absent instrument, and no ping was used at any point.
